---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Salary Negotiation Guides | salarynegotiationcalc.com';
const description = 'In-depth guides on salary negotiation: how to negotiate, salary research, job offer conversations, and common misconceptions — reviewed by editorial staff.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Salary Negotiation Guides</h1>
  <p>Plain-language guides written and reviewed by editorial staff with experience in compensation strategy and career negotiation. Each guide provides the practical and psychological context behind effective salary negotiation.</p>

  <h2><a href="/guides/how-to-negotiate-salary">How to Negotiate Salary</a></h2>
  <p>Step-by-step guide to negotiating a job offer or merit increase: research, timing, anchoring, handling pushback, and negotiating total compensation beyond base salary. Covers the complete negotiation conversation from first offer to final acceptance.</p>

  <h2><a href="/guides/salary-research-guide">Salary Research Guide</a></h2>
  <p>How to use Glassdoor, Levels.fyi, LinkedIn Salary, BLS data, and peer network intelligence to build a defensible salary ask. Covers how to read salary bands, adjust for location, and identify where in a company&rsquo;s pay range you should be targeting.</p>

  <h2><a href="/guides/negotiating-job-offers">Negotiating Job Offers</a></h2>
  <p>The specific mechanics of the offer negotiation conversation: how to evaluate an offer, structure a counter, handle multiple competing offers, manage the emotional dynamics, and accept or decline professionally. Covers what to say, when to say it, and when to stop.</p>

  <h2><a href="/guides/salary-negotiation-misconceptions">Common Salary Negotiation Misconceptions</a></h2>
  <p>Five widely held misunderstandings about salary negotiation: that it is rude or aggressive, that offers can be rescinded for asking, that current salary caps future offers, that benefits should wait until after joining, and that posted salary ranges represent the ceiling.</p>

  <ul style="margin-top:2rem">
    <li><a href="/case-types">Negotiation types overview</a> — new offers, reviews, promotions, equity, counter-offers</li>
    <li><a href="/methodology">Calculator methodology</a> — documented industry multipliers and location premiums</li>
    <li><a href="/faq">FAQ</a> — salary history laws, competing offers, total compensation components</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Return to the <a href="/">calculator</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
